msgid "Without version control, versions of a program look like this: `report.sas`, `report_v2.sas`, `report_v2_final.sas`, `report_v2_final_MARIA.sas`. Which one made last month's numbers? What changed between them?"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-modules-and-git.md:1104
msgid "**Git** keeps the full history of a project folder:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-modules-and-git.md:1106
msgid "every saved version (**commit**) with its date, author and a message;"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-modules-and-git.md:1107
msgid "what changed in each one, line by line;"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-modules-and-git.md:1108
msgid "the way back to any earlier version;"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-modules-and-git.md:1109
msgid "parallel lines of work (**branches**) that can be merged."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-modules-and-git.md:1111
msgid "Git runs on your computer (you installed it for [session 1](./01-intro-syntax-types.md)). **GitHub**, GitLab and Azure DevOps are websites that keep a copy of a repository, for sharing and backup (section 8)."
msgstr ""

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/09-modules-and-git.md:1115
msgid "Three places"
